# .dev.vars.example — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT variables (Wrangler reads .dev.vars)
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in REAL values for local testing only:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# NEVER commit `.dev.vars` (it is in .gitignore) and NEVER paste real values
# into GitHub, chat, or any file in this repository.
#
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH — PBKDF2-SHA256 hash of the admin password.
# Format: pbkdf2$<iterations>$<salt base64>$<hash base64>
# Generate it by opening scripts/make-hash.html in a browser and typing the
# password there. Example format only (NOT a real hash):
ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=pbkdf2$100000$REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_SALT$REPLACE_WITH_BASE64_HASH
#
# SESSION_SECRET — long random string (at least 32 characters). Used as a pepper
# when hashing session tokens before storing them in D1. Generate with, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Example placeholder only (NOT a real secret):
SESSION_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_A_LONG_RANDOM_STRING_AT_LEAST_32_CHARS
#
# RATE_LIMIT_SALT — optional. Extra salt mixed into rate-limit IP hashes.
# If left empty, a built-in default is used. Any random string is fine.
RATE_LIMIT_SALT=
